========================================================================================================================
                                       VIRSH STORAGE COMMANDS REFERENCE MANUAL
========================================================================================================================

COMMAND         | DESCRIPTION                                           | PRACTICAL EXAMPLE
----------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------
pool-list       | Lists active and/or inactive storage pools.          | virsh pool-list --all
pool-define-as  | Configures a persistent pool using command arguments. | virsh pool-define-as local-dir dir --target /data/storage
pool-build      | Prepares the underlying storage source (e.g. format). | virsh pool-build local-dir
pool-start      | Activates an inactive predefined storage pool.       | virsh pool-start local-dir
pool-destroy    | Force-stops an active storage pool immediately.       | virsh pool-destroy local-dir
pool-undefine   | Deletes the configuration of an inactive pool.       | virsh pool-undefine local-dir
pool-delete     | Deletes the actual underlying storage directory/disk. | virsh pool-delete local-dir
pool-dumpxml    | Exports pool configuration to standard XML output.    | virsh pool-dumpxml local-dir > pool_backup.xml
pool-edit       | Opens pool XML configuration in default text editor.  | virsh pool-edit local-dir
pool-autostart  | Configures a pool to start automatically at boot.     | virsh pool-autostart local-dir
pool-info       | Displays pool state, capacity, allocation, available.| virsh pool-info local-dir
pool-refresh    | Refreshes and updates the list of volumes in a pool.  | virsh pool-refresh local-dir
----------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------
vol-list        | Lists all storage volumes within a specific pool.    | virsh vol-list local-dir
vol-create-as   | Creates a new virtual disk volume inside a pool.      | virsh vol-create-as local-dir web_disk.qcow2 20G --format qcow2
vol-clone       | Clones an existing storage volume into a new one.     | virsh vol-clone --pool local-dir ubuntu.qcow2 new_vm.qcow2
vol-delete      | Deletes a specific storage volume from a pool.        | virsh vol-delete --pool local-dir web_disk.qcow2
vol-resize      | Expands or shrinks the capacity of a storage volume.   | virsh vol-resize --pool local-dir web_disk.qcow2 30G
vol-info        | Displays volume type, capacity, and allocation details| virsh vol-info --pool local-dir web_disk.qcow2
vol-path        | Returns the absolute OS path of a storage volume.     | virsh vol-path --pool local-dir web_disk.qcow2
vol-dumpxml     | Exports volume configuration details to XML format.   | virsh vol-dumpxml --pool local-dir web_disk.qcow2
